 <nav class="publication-toc" aria-label="Table of contents"><h2>On this page</h2><a href="#verdict">Verdict</a><a href="#what">What Freshdesk does</a><a href="#pricing">Pricing</a><a href="#features">Key features</a><a href="#strengths">Strengths and trade-offs</a><a href="#fit">Who it fits</a><a href="#alternatives">Alternatives</a><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
 <article class="publication-body"><details class="publication-mobile-toc"><summary>On this page</summary><a href="#verdict">Verdict</a><a href="#what">What Freshdesk does</a><a href="#pricing">Pricing</a><a href="#features">Key features</a><a href="#strengths">Strengths and trade-offs</a><a href="#fit">Who it fits</a><a href="#alternatives">Alternatives</a><a href="#faq">Frequently asked questions</a><a href="#sources">Review methodology and sources</a></details>
  <p class="publication-lead">Freshdesk is a good option for teams that want an email-first help desk with ticket ownership, automation, a customer portal and a knowledge base. Its entry paid plan is listed at US$19 per agent/month with annual billing, but AI usage and plan-level controls can change the total cost. Confirm whether standard Freshdesk or Freshdesk Omni matches your channel needs before buying.</p>
  <div class="publication-summary"><h2 id="verdict">Verdict at a glance</h2><ul><li><strong>Best for:</strong> teams that manage most support through email and want tickets, collaboration and self-service in one workspace.</li><li><strong>Starting price:</strong> Growth at US$19 per agent/month billed annually. Checked October 28, 2026. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Official pricing</a>.</li><li><strong>Free access:</strong> the US pricing page advertises a 14-day trial. Freshworks support docs also describe a six-month Free Program for eligible Freshdesk customers, limited to two agents and not available in Freshdesk Omni. It is not a permanent free tier; confirm eligibility in your account. <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/50000010099-explore-freshdesk-free-program-freshdesk-only-">Official Free Program guide</a>.</li><li><strong>Main limit to check:</strong> channel coverage, advanced routing and dashboards depend on the product and plan. AI usage can add charges.</li></ul></div>
  <h2 id="what">What Freshdesk actually is</h2>
  <p>Freshdesk is Freshworks' email-first customer support product. It organizes customer requests as tickets and gives teams tools for assignment, collaboration, automation, reporting and self-service. The customer portal and knowledge base can help customers find answers without opening a new ticket, provided the articles are accurate and easy to find.</p>
  <p>Freshdesk is not the same as Freshdesk Omni. Freshworks describes standard Freshdesk as email-first, with core ticketing, collaboration and automation. Freshdesk Omni adds broader channel coverage in a unified inbox, including chat and social messaging. The distinction matters because an Omni workflow should not be priced using a standard Freshdesk plan. The <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/50000011785-getting-started-with-freshdesk-omni">official onboarding guide</a> explains the current product differences.</p>
  <h2 id="pricing">Pricing and the real cost</h2>
  <p>The official US pricing page lists Growth at US$19, Pro at US$55 and Enterprise at US$89 per agent/month with annual billing. These prices were <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">checked on October 28, 2026</a>. They are monthly equivalents for annual billing, not month-to-month totals. Check the <a href="/freshdesk/pricing/">Freshdesk pricing guide</a> for the plan table and cost examples.</p>
  <div class="publication-table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">Published price</th><th scope="col">Decision note</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Growth</th><td>US$19 per agent/month, billed annually. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Checked on October 28, 2026</a>.</td><td>Core ticketing, customer portal, knowledge and reporting needs.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pro</th><td>US$55 per agent/month, billed annually. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Checked on October 28, 2026</a>.</td><td>More routing, dashboards and SLA control.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Enterprise</th><td>US$89 per agent/month, billed annually. <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">Checked on October 28, 2026</a>.</td><td>Additional administration and enterprise workflow controls.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <p>Do not budget from the seat price alone. The pricing page lists the first 500 Freddy AI Agent sessions as included, with additional sessions at US$49 per 100, and Freddy AI Copilot at US$29 per agent/month on eligible Pro and Enterprise plans. These details were <a href="https://www.freshworks.com/freshdesk/pricing/">checked on October 28, 2026</a>. Confirm how sessions are counted, when the included allowance resets and whether every agent needs Copilot.</p>
  <p>The public pricing page advertises a 14-day trial. Freshworks support docs also describe a separate six-month Free Program for eligible Freshdesk customers, limited to two agents and not available in Freshdesk Omni. It is not a permanent free tier, so confirm the current eligibility and terms in your account. Read the <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/50000010099-explore-freshdesk-free-program-freshdesk-only-">official Free Program guide</a>, checked <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/50000010099-explore-freshdesk-free-program-freshdesk-only-">October 28, 2026</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="features">Key features worth evaluating</h2>
  <h3>1. Ticketing and shared ownership</h3>
  <p>Freshdesk puts requests into tickets so a team can assign, prioritize and track work. This is useful when a shared inbox has become difficult to manage because ownership is unclear. The quality of the setup depends on clear groups, ticket fields and escalation rules. Too many fields or overlapping automation rules can make the workflow harder to use.</p>
  <h3>2. Support email setup</h3>
  <p>Freshworks documents a current setup flow for support addresses and the mail server options. Incoming messages can become tickets when the address is connected correctly. Use the <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/37541-set-up-your-support-email">official support email guide</a> rather than copying settings from an old tutorial. Test a message from an external account and confirm that replies stay attached to the ticket.</p>
  <h3>3. Automation and routing</h3>
  <p>Freshdesk supports ticket creation rules that can apply actions when a new request matches defined conditions. For example, a billing request can be assigned to a billing group. Freshworks' <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/37614-managing-tickets-using-the-dispatch-r">official automation guide</a> explains how to configure rules. Start with a small set of rules and test both matching and non-matching tickets before enabling them for the full queue.</p>
  <h3>4. Service-level targets</h3>
  <p>SLA policies set response or resolution targets for ticket types and priorities. They help teams make service expectations explicit, but only if business hours, holidays and ticket conditions are configured correctly. The <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/37626">official SLA guide</a>, modified August 20, 2026, describes the current behavior and plan requirements. Confirm the exact controls in your account.</p>
  <h3>5. Customer portal and knowledge base</h3>
  <p>Self-service can reduce repeat questions when articles answer real customer problems. A useful help article should state the answer early, list the required permissions and provide steps the reader can follow. Freshdesk's portal and knowledge capabilities are worth evaluating if customers often ask the same setup, billing or account questions. The result depends on content quality as much as the tool.</p>
  <h3>6. Reporting and AI</h3>
  <p>Freshdesk lists reporting on its entry paid plan and custom dashboards on Pro. Higher plans add more controls. AI features can help agents or automate some responses, but the price model matters: an included session allowance, paid additional sessions and a Copilot add-on should be calculated separately. Ask the vendor for an example based on your ticket volume.</p>
  <h3>7. Data export</h3>
  <p>Freshdesk documents CSV and Excel exports for tickets, contacts, companies and other account data. The <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/225158">official export guide</a> says an Admin or Supervisor role and the right export permissions are required. Export capability is useful for audits and migrations, but it does not prove that every comment, attachment, custom field or workflow will import into another product without changes.</p>
  <h2 id="strengths">Strengths and trade-offs</h2>
  <div class="publication-pros-cons"><section><h3>Potential strengths</h3><ul><li>Clear entry pricing for the standard email-first product.</li><li>Ticketing, groups and automation for repeatable ownership.</li><li>Customer portal and knowledge base for self-service.</li><li>Documented ticket and account data exports.</li><li>A trial to evaluate the workflow before committing.</li></ul></section><section><h3>Trade-offs to check</h3><ul><li>Standard Freshdesk and Freshdesk Omni have different channel coverage.</li><li>Advanced routing and dashboard controls may require a higher plan.</li><li>AI sessions and Copilot can add usage or seat costs.</li><li>The current public pricing page does not show a self-serve permanent free plan for new signups.</li><li>Export files do not automatically recreate another help desk's rules, reports or workflows.</li></ul></section></div>
  <h2 id="fit">Who should use Freshdesk?</h2>
  <p>Freshdesk is worth a shortlist if email is the main support channel and the team wants to move beyond separate inboxes. It can fit businesses that need clear ticket ownership, customer-facing help content, basic automation and a reporting routine. It is also worth testing if a team needs to organize a growing queue without immediately buying a broad enterprise service suite.</p>
  <p>Look elsewhere if a required channel is not included in the product you are pricing, if you need a specific routing or reporting control that is not available in the chosen tier, or if your organization depends on a CRM or ecommerce workflow that another platform handles more directly. If the cost of AI is central to the decision, estimate the likely sessions and agent seats before you decide.</p>
  <h2 id="alternatives">Alternatives to compare</h2>
  <p>Start with <a href="/freshdesk/alternatives/">Freshdesk alternatives</a> if the plan, channel set or cost model does not fit. <a href="/zendesk/review/">Zendesk</a> is the closest direct comparison for structured ticketing and a broader suite. <a href="https://www.helpscout.com/">Help Scout</a> suits teams that prefer a shared inbox and help center, while <a href="https://www.zoho.com/desk/">Zoho Desk</a> is worth checking for small teams and existing Zoho users. If you are choosing between the two products, read the <a href="/compare/zendesk-vs-freshdesk/">Zendesk vs Freshdesk comparison</a>.</p>
  <h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <h3>How much does Freshdesk cost?</h3><p>The US pricing page checked October 28, 2026 lists Growth at US$19, Pro at US$55 and Enterprise at US$89 per agent/month with annual billing. AI usage and optional features can add cost.</p>
  <h3>Is Freshdesk free?</h3><p>The US pricing page advertises a 14-day trial. Freshworks also documents a six-month Free Program for eligible Freshdesk customers, limited to two agents and not available in Freshdesk Omni. It is not a permanent free tier; confirm eligibility in your account. Read the <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/50000010099-explore-freshdesk-free-program-freshdesk-only-">official Free Program guide</a>, checked <a href="https://support.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/50000010099-explore-freshdesk-free-program-freshdesk-only-">October 28, 2026</a>.</p>
  <h3>What is the difference between Freshdesk and Freshdesk Omni?</h3><p>Freshdesk is email-first. Freshdesk Omni supports a broader set of channels in a unified inbox. Check the current product matrix before comparing plans.</p>
  <h3>Can Freshdesk tickets be exported?</h3><p>Yes. Freshdesk documents CSV and Excel exports for tickets and other records. An Admin or Supervisor role and export permissions are required.</p>
  <h3>Does this review include hands-on testing?</h3><p>No. It is a research-based review using official product, pricing, help-center and product-update pages checked October 28, 2026.</p>
  <h2 id="sources">Review methodology and sources</h2>
  <p>This review uses official product, pricing, support and product-update pages checked October 28, 2026. It does not claim hands-on testing, customer interviews or independent performance benchmarks. Prices and plan details can change; verify them before purchase.</p>
